## Intuition
Since the array is already sorted, all duplicate elements will be next to each other. We can use a two-pointer approach to keep track of the position where the next unique element should be placed.

## Approach 
We start with **index = 1** because the first element is always unique. Then, we traverse the array from the second element. If the current element is different from the previous element, it is a unique element, so we place it at **nums[index]** and increment **index**. Finally, **index** represents the number of unique elements in the array.


